\section*{Injectivity of the Baum–Connes Assembly Map}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
For one finitely generated group without torsion, the coefficient-free reduced assembly map annihilates an infinite-order degree-zero K-homology class; this is claimed to refute rational injectivity. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 285, 2026-09-23): The construction embeds a torus subgroup with an integral cohomology detector while arranging disappearance of its Bott class analytically. Operators assembled on almost disjoint Cayley-graph sheets retain controlled spectral supports; estimates for the leftover forest permit the required homotopies in the reduced completion. A finite witness then restricts the construction to a finitely generated subgroup.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 285, 2026-09-23): The infinite-order degree-zero assembly-kernel class for a finitely generated torsion-free discrete group directly refutes the universal coefficient-free reduced injectivity and isomorphism assertions, with no coefficient or maximal-completion substitution.

\subsection{Formal verification}
Family 285 has no Lean scope page in this snapshot; no formalization of these manuscript results is listed.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item OpenAI, \emph{A torsion-free counterexample to reduced Baum–Connes injectivity}, 2026-09-23; citation key \texttt{OAI:A-Torsion-Free-Counterexample-to-Reduced-Baum-Connes-Injectivity-September-23-2026}. \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-Torsion-Free-Counterexample-to-Reduced-Baum-Connes-Injectivity-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (GitHub)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/raw/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-Torsion-Free-Counterexample-to-Reduced-Baum-Connes-Injectivity-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (direct)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-Torsion-Free-Counterexample-to-Reduced-Baum-Connes-Injectivity-September-23-2026/README.md}{Manuscript page and citation}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/A-Torsion-Free-Counterexample-to-Reduced-Baum-Connes-Injectivity-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{Latest version}.
